--- a/.andromeda/security-plan.md
+++ b/.andromeda/security-plan.md
@@ -13,3 +13,3 @@
 decision/driver-session-unix-socket-only · Driver session on one Unix socket — The driver session binds one Unix-domain socket in a caller-named state directory, never a TCP or UDP port, and runs on unix only.
-decision/file-url-only-for-file-documents · File URLs load only for file documents — A file: URL loads only for a file: document; for any other document, remote pages included, JS fetch, module import and script src alike refuse it with a FetchError.
+decision/file-url-only-for-file-documents · File URLs load only for file documents — A file: URL loads only for a file: document or a top-level load; for any other document, remote pages included, JS fetch, module import and script src refuse it with a FetchError, and blitz-net refuses the engine's stylesheet, @import, font, image and iframe loads before any disk read.
 decision/graph-answer-crossing · Graph answer crossing — A graph answer carries the screen's UI graph on the socket, the command line, MCP and a kept check: ids, owner ids, component names, registered state names, handler event names, closed flag words and booleans, never a control value, typed text or NodeId. · why: A boundary widening, ratified.
@@ -110,3 +110,3 @@
 decision/fetch-get-head-only · Script fetch limited to GET and HEAD — A page script's fetch rejects with TypeError any method other than GET or HEAD.
-decision/file-urls-only-from-file-documents · file URLs load only from file documents — A script fetch, a module import or a script src may load a file: URL only for a file: document, in every document, remote pages included. · why: A narrowing, not a boundary widening. · guard: remote_document_cannot_load_file_urls
+decision/file-urls-only-from-file-documents · file URLs load only from file documents — A script fetch, module import or script src, and every engine stylesheet, @import, font, image or iframe load, may read a file: URL only for a file: document or a top-level load, in every document, remote pages included; blitz-net refuses any other before a disk read. · why: A narrowing, not a boundary widening. · guard: remote_document_cannot_load_file_urls
 decision/hintless-font-face-source-sniffed · Hint-less font-face source fetched and sniffed — An @font-face source whose URL cannot be resolved is skipped; a source with no format hint and no extension is fetched and its format sniffed from its bytes. · why: Ratified as upstream's behaviour, with a check asked for. · guard: font_face_sniffed_source
@@ -143,2 +143,3 @@
 decision/one-command-span-per-call · One command span per call — Every call handed to the session is wrapped in one INFO span named command under the escher_driver target, entered before validation so a refusal is inside it, holding fixed words, booleans and counts only.
+decision/one-stamping-request-constructor · One stamping constructor for sub-resource requests — blitz-dom builds a sub-resource request only through the one constructor that stamps its loading document as the request's initiator. · why: Upstream's blitz-dom has no such lint config, so the rule is a new upstream merge surface. · guard: blitz-dom's clippy disallowed-methods rule on Request::get · except: The stamping constructor itself, under a single expect.
 decision/one-validation-path-for-every-carrier · One validation path for every carrier — The session socket, the command line and MCP each pass a call through the schema's validation before anything runs, and nothing public runs a command that did not come from that validation. · why: The crossing to external input surfaces was ratified with this check as the one they all pass through.
@@ -493,2 +494,3 @@
 decision/try-doc-none-while-borrowed · try_doc answers none while the document is borrowed — Event handling may ask for the document while it is mutably borrowed and gets None instead of a panic. · why: The browser status bar reads the document through try_doc and returns early instead of panicking while event handling holds the borrow
+contract/blitz-net-provider-error/file-forbidden · blitz-net provider errors · FileForbidden — The refusal of a file: load for a non-file document has the fixed display text «file: load refused for a non-file document», holding no URL or path, and reaches the handler only through the existing error path with no log site of its own.
 contract/cli-exit-codes/1 · escher-session CLI exit codes · 1 — The call was refused; the refusal JSON is written to stdout.
